# No Hard-Wrapping in Markdown

Do not insert manual line breaks to wrap prose at a fixed column width. Write each paragraph as one continuous line and let the editor soft-wrap it. Hard wraps create noisy diffs and break reflow.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD: manual line breaks mid-sentence -->
The house chat is the blueprint for the later Aura chat. The difference is that Aura
will have a larger context and more tools, and it will be usable by everyone, not
just developers.

<!-- ✅ GOOD: one line per paragraph, soft-wrapped by the editor -->
The house chat is the blueprint for the later Aura chat. The difference is that Aura will have a larger context and more tools, and it will be usable by everyone, not just developers.
```

Line breaks are only allowed where they carry meaning: between paragraphs, list items, table rows, headings, and inside fenced code blocks.
